.TH MD_UNPIN_FREQUENCY 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_unpin_frequency \- release the current channel pin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_unpin_frequency(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Release the current channel pin.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
decoder is NULL or the stream has been flushed.
.SH REMARKS
Clears the pin on the current channel if one exists. No current channel, or a
current channel that is already unpinned, is a successful no-op. The existing
selection and message are retained immediately; future processing may switch
or retire that channel under the normal automatic rules.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_pin_frequency (3),
.BR md_set_frequency (3),
.BR md_get_state (3)
